            "bg_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "title": "H2 To reduce pollen allergy symptoms:",
            "title_style": "h2"
          }
        },
        "richtext_3GWnj7": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "spacing_top_mobile": 24,
            "spacing_bottom_mobile": 24,
            "spacing_top_desktop": 24,
            "spacing_bottom_desktop": 24,
            "bg_color": "#f0f3f6",
            "richtext": "<p>Monitor your local pollen count! Local newspapers and TV news websites often publish daily reports. Stay indoors as much as you can, especially during peak hours (usually mid-morning to early afternoon) and keep your doors and windows closed.</p>",
            "richtext_style": "text-p2"
          }
        },
        "bullet_dQNt6z": {
          "type": "bullet",
          "settings": {
            "spacing_top_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_top_desktop": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_desktop": 8,
            "bg_color": "#f0f3f6",
            "text": "When you do go outside, wear a mask to filter pollen.",
            "text_style": "text-p2"
          }
        },
        "bullet_rBHNYD": {
          "type": "bullet",
          "settings": {
            "spacing_top_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_top_desktop": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_desktop": 8,
            "bg_color": "#f0f3f6",
            "text": "When driving, keep your windows completely closed, and when you return home, remove your shoes and jacket before going inside. You don’t want to bring any pollen that you’ve picked up outside into your home.",
            "text_style": "text-p2"
          }
        },
        "bullet_39tWNC": {
          "type": "bullet",
          "settings": {
            "spacing_top_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_top_desktop": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_desktop": 8,
            "bg_color": "#f0f3f6",
            "text": "Vacuum carpets and upholstery regularly, and wash your clothes, linens, and curtains regularly. After you’ve washed your clothes, avoid drying them on a line outdoors.",
            "text_style": "text-p2"
          }
        },
        "bullet_rFkbbW": {
          "type": "bullet",
          "settings": {
            "spacing_top_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_mobile": 8,
            "spacing_top_desktop": 8,
            "spacing_bottom_desktop": 8,
            "bg_color": "#f0f3f6",
            "text": "Do you have pets? They may not agree with this, but you should bathe them frequently. Especially dogs and cats that spend time outdoors.",
            "text_style": "text-p2"
          }
        }
      },
